# Armv9 SME (FEAT_SME), SME2 (FEAT_SME2), SME2.1 and SME2.2, with the SME
# F64F64, I16I64, F16F16, B16B16, F8F16, F8F32, LUTv2, MOP4 and TMOP extensions.
#
# Generated by tools/gen_aarch64_ext.py, as AARCH64_sve2.sinc: the encodings come
# from LLVM's AArch64 TableGen instruction records whose predicates name these
# features (records also predicated on an SVE2 feature are in AARCH64_sve2.sinc);
# mnemonics, operand order and operand text come from LLVM's disassembler
# (llvm-mc -M no-aliases), field value by field value. The ZA array and ZT0 are
# not varnodes: a ZA tile, tile slice or array vector is passed to the user
# operation as its encoded number together with its index registers and
# immediates. Every instruction lifts to a user operation named after its
# mnemonic (SME_<mnemonic>); its output is the Z, P or general register it
# writes (the first of a register list), and an instruction that writes ZA takes
# the ZA operand as its first input instead.

